      "adaptation": {
        "semantic": "**Go** is movement away from the speaker's place; **come** is movement toward the speaker or the listener. Languages that lack this line often use **go** where English needs **come**: *I will come to your party.*",
        "grammar": "No preposition before **home**, **there**, **abroad**, or **upstairs**: *go home*. Activities take the -ing form with no **to**: *go swimming*, not *go to swim*. **School**, **work**, **church**, and **bed** take **to** with no article when the purpose is the usual one: *go to school*.",
        "culture": null,
